---
// The VCF 9 model as stacked blocks: the fleet on top, instances beneath it, domains inside each instance. Same
// content as the diagram in the note "The VCF 9 mental model". Real text in CSS blocks, not an SVG, so it reflows on
// a phone and stays at reading size. Only the support clock is drawn; this figure is set in solid tone.
---
<figure class="fleet">
  <figcaption>VCF 9 puts a fleet and instances above the domains you knew from 5.x. <a href="/vcf/library/architecture/vcf9-mental-model/">Read the note</a></figcaption>
  <div class="fm">
    <div class="fm-fleet">
      <span class="fm-l">Fleet</span>
      <b>VCF Operations · VCF Automation</b>
      <span class="fm-d">Console, licensing, identity and fleet lifecycle</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fm-insts">
      <div class="fm-inst n3">
        <span class="fm-name">Instance 1</span>
        <div class="fm-doms">
          <div class="fm-dom m"><b>Management domain</b>SDDC Manager<br />vCenter · NSX<br />Services runtime</div>
          <div class="fm-dom"><b>Workload domain</b>vCenter · NSX</div>
          <div class="fm-dom"><b>Workload domain</b>vCenter · NSX</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="fm-inst n2">
        <span class="fm-name">Instance 2</span>
        <div class="fm-doms">
          <div class="fm-dom m"><b>Management domain</b>SDDC Manager<br />vCenter · NSX<br />Services runtime</div>
          <div class="fm-dom"><b>Workload domains</b>One vCenter each,<br />NSX own or shared</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</figure>
